    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "II — Orchestration",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "A manager agent hands specialized work to a researcher, a writer, a validator — and all of them read and write one shared store. That store is the whole pattern. Two agents writing at once without locks corrupts it, so each gets a read-only snapshot and submits an atomic patch the orchestrator validates.",
      "new_visual_element": "Multi-agent collaboration — the shared store",
