    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "III — Memory",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "Memory is a classification problem before it is a storage problem. Conversation goes to short-term and gets compressed. Events go to a vector store tagged with recency. Core preferences get extracted into a structured profile that never decays. And retrieval scores on similarity, recency and frequency together — never similarity alone.",
      "new_visual_element": "Memory management — the three tiers",
