    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "III — Memory",
      "estimated_duration_s": 21,
      "narration_text": "Capture feedback, denoise it, then update behaviour. The denoise step is the one people skip. Feedback is noisy and sometimes malicious, so a system that learns from all of it learns the wrong thing. And prefer rewriting prompts and swapping examples over fine-tuning — real-time fine-tuning is rare and risky.",
